</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Reproducibility Details</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Computational Budget and Infrastructure</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All of our experiments are inference-only; we do not perform any model training or fine-tuning. The only learning step is the lightweight optimization of per-stream calibrators and routing thresholds, which runs on CPU and adds negligible cost. Model inference was conducted on a single NVIDIA H200 NVL (141GB) GPU. The full set of experiments (fourteen models across five benchmarks, six debater pairs per benchmark, with self-consistency sampling of three generations per query) can be reproduced on a single NVIDIA H200 GPU in 18 days, considering the five statistical significance test runs. Parameter counts for all models follow their officially released sizes (3B–32B), listed in the Experimental setup section.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Datasets and Statistics</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate on five publicly available English benchmarks spanning four task types. Table <a href="#A1.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ A.2 Datasets and Statistics ‣ Appendix A Reproducibility Details ‣ Multiagent Protocols with Aggregated Confidence Signals" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> reports the task, label space, and the split sizes used in our experiments. For every dataset, we use a held-out validation split to fit calibrators and learn routing thresholds, and report all results on the test split; the validation split is never used for evaluation. The training set is never used in general. We only used the college sections of the MMLU dataset.</p>
</div>
